Aerie-Purpose: Put the "Put inactive tabs to sleep after" row in the Sidebar section of Settings, and give the page its strings.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/resources/settings (appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.ts, appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.html.ts, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings (settings_localized_strings_provider.cc)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #179. The row, settings-aerie-sleep-row, is a Lit element in the overlay
(chrome/browser/resources/settings/appearance_page/aerie_sleep_row.*). It is a
settings-dropdown-menu on the pref aerie.tabs.sleep_after_minutes (patches/sidebar/0010, already in
the settings_private allowlist as a number), with the options 15 min, 30 min, 1 h (default), 2 h,
4 h, 8 h and Never. Its strings are in the overlay's aerie_sidebar_strings.grdp, which
patches/sidebar/0022 includes in generated_resources.grd; this patch hands them to the page. The
element sits in the "Sidebar" section that patches/sidebar/0022 made.

